;; kasa 嵩 — seed of WORLDWIDE COMPUTING-CAPACITY observations (public information only)
;; ADR-2606072000 · vocabulary: compute-capacity-ontology.kotoba.edn (00-contracts/schemas/)
;;
;; SCOPE: a bounded illustrative slice of the world's annual computing-capacity magnitude + growth
;;   across the four domains the founder named — STORAGE (HDD+SSD exabytes shipped), MEMORY (DRAM +
;;   NAND revenue), GPU/CPU (discrete-GPU + client-CPU units, datacenter-accelerator revenue) and
;;   COMPUTE/FLOPS (TOP500 aggregate, frontier training compute) — plus DATACENTER power capacity.
;;   Demonstrates: (1) one EAVT vocabulary spanning revenue / capacity / units / FLOPS / watts,
;;   (2) the four sourcing tiers (:representative headline · :estimated nowcast · :synthesized
;;   derived), (3) YoY + CAGR growth (the founder's 年間増加量), (4) coverage-honest aggregates that
;;   never double-count memory inside semiconductor.
;;
;; SOURCING (G5): every observation here is :representative (publicly-documented HEADLINE figures
;;   from WSTS/SIA + TrendForce + IDC + JPR press releases and the public TOP500 list), ROUNDED —
;;   NOT the exact dataset row. The two derived/estimated series — frontier TRAINING compute and
;;   DATACENTER power capacity — are :estimated (analyst/Epoch-AI estimates of a knowable-but-not-
;;   directly-reported quantity), each carrying a :compute.obs/method. The authoritative path parses
;;   the actual press-release table / open CSV (G7 operator-gated, ingest.py). Absence of a year =
;;   "not yet ingested", NOT "zero". These are PAST/PRESENT actuals — kasa does NOT forecast (G4).
;;
;; NON-ADJUDICATING (G2) / PLANNING-LENS (G9): these are quantities the world measured. kasa records
;;   them to SIZE the compute commons; it does NOT rank countries/companies "ahead/behind", build an
;;   export-control / targeting list, or give investment advice.

